1 REFN anna_haesaerts
2 TYPE project-id
1 NAME Anna /Haesaerts/
2 GIVN Anna
2 SURN Haesaerts
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 24 OCT 1810
2 PLAC Bertem
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 JAN 1880
2 PLAC Bertem
1 OCCU landbouwster (farmer)
1 FAMS @F36@
1 FAMC @F40@
1 NOTE Mother of the bride in her daughter [[coekelberghs]]'s marriage act — Sint-Stevens-Woluwe
2 CONT nr. 6, 24 April 1873. A *landbouwster* of Bertem, present and consenting, and like her
2 CONT husband [[jb_coekelberghs]] recorded as unable to write or sign.
2 CONT
2 CONT Named again in the same daughter's 1903 Kraainem remarriage act, which gives her death:
2 CONT Bertem, 8 January 1880 — ten months before her husband, and both of them nine years dead
2 CONT when their son-in-law died at Kraainem.
2 CONT
2 CONT The act gives her no age, so this record carries no birth date.
2 CONT
2 CONT `sup`: AGATHA act analyses, not the register images.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER — **her forename is unstable across the acts, and it is not settled here.** The
2 CONT 1838 Bertem marriage, the 1853 birth, the 1873 marriage and the 1903 marriage all write
2 CONT her *Anna Haesaerts* plain; two 1867 acts write *Anna Maria Haesaerts*; an 1858 birth
2 CONT writes *Anna Catharina Haesaerts*. One husband, one commune, one occupation and an
2 CONT unbroken run of children from 1839 to 1858 make one woman written three ways much the
2 CONT likeliest reading — but it is a reading, not a fact, and the records are deliberately
2 CONT **not merged** on it. Only the register images, or her own death act at Bertem in January
2 CONT 1880, will settle which forename she was baptised with.
2 CONT
2 CONT GRAFTED (2026-07-26) — her own marriage act, **Bertem nr. 8, 30 October 1838, read as the
2 CONT register image** (`fs-bertem-1838-marriage-register-nr8`). It gives her birth, **Bertem
2 CONT 24 October 1810** — where this record had none — and her parents [[jb_haesaerts]] and
2 CONT [[elisabeth_vdbroeck]], both *landbouwers* of Berthem, both present and consenting in
2 CONT person, and both, like her, unable to sign. The image corrects two of AGATHA's spellings:
2 CONT *Joannes Baptista* Haesaerts, not *Baptist*, and *van den Broeck* in three words.
2 CONT
2 CONT **On the forename, the act settles less than it looks.** She is written plain **Anna**
2 CONT three times — twice in the display hand opening her half of the act, and again in the
2 CONT operative sentence — with no second forename and no gap where one was dropped. So *Anna*
2 CONT is what she was called at her own wedding. It is not what she was baptised: a birth act
2 CONT would say that, and the 1838 act reports her birth rather than proving it. *Anna Maria*
2 CONT (two 1867 acts) and *Anna Catharina* (an 1858 birth) therefore stay **unreconciled and
2 CONT unmerged**, exactly as before. Her Bertem birth of 24 October 1810 is now a dated, single
2 CONT target instead of a range, and that is the test.
2 CONT
2 CONT `sup`, not `doc`, for the same reason as [[jb_coekelberghs]]: the image proves the 1838
2 CONT act, not that its bride is [[coekelberghs]]'s mother, and that bridge is two AGATHA
2 CONT transcriptions.
1 SOUR @S17@
2 QUAY 2
