2 NOTE Recorded as: Zaventem/Leuven, a few years ago
1 FAMS @F48@
1 NOTE Van Craenenbroeck is, in Zaventem, essentially ONE extended family, and it is richly documented — back to a 1721 marriage in Zaventem, and through the 1800s in neighbouring Sterrebeek, Wezembeek-Oppem and Kraainem. FAMILY LOCATED (Geneanet, July 2026): the modern Zaventem trunk (Geneanet tree 'cisken' + the Zaventem Kerkhoflaan cemetery index) centres on Antonius Josephus Van Craenenbroeck (1872 Sterrebeek – 1936 Zaventem) × Anna Maria Meeus (1877–1957) — Antonius himself a son of Amandus Franciscus Van Craenenbroeck (1835–1914) × Paulina Mommaerts (1838–1909), so this family is now documented back to the 1830s — with a sibling set born in Zaventem 1902–1918: Amandus Franciscus Henricus (1902–1977, m. Maria Balcaen 1929), Paul Gustaaf (1904–1988, m. Joanna Smolders 1928), Melania Leonia (1906), Joannes Arthur (1908–1982, m. Roza Van Opstal), Maurice Louis Willem (1913–1991) and Bertha Rosalia (1918). Anna — Chris & Eric's mother, born ~1930s in Zaventem, the witloof-farming milieu — fits this family almost certainly (rare surname + exact village + occupation region) and is most plausibly a GRANDDAUGHTER of Antonius, i.e. a daughter of one of those ~1928–29-married couples (Paul Gustaaf × Smolders or Amandus × Balcaen are the leading candidates). BUT the specific parent is NOT yet documented — the 'cisken' tree stops just above Anna's generation — so it is left OPEN, not grafted (no father/mother set here). To confirm which sibling is her parent: (1) Anna's own death notice / memorial card (she died recently in the Zaventem/Leuven area — likely names her parents and siblings); (2) her grave in the Zaventem Kerkhoflaan index; or (3) the owner of the 'cisken' Geneanet tree, a relative who very likely holds Anna's generation privately. Any one of these closes the link.
