1 OCCU arbeider (labourer)
1 FAMS @F42@
1 NOTE Father of the groom in his son [[guilielmus_bossin]]'s marriage act — Zaventem, act nr.
2 CONT 1, 24 February 1846 (S19), read as an image. The act puts him at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe,
2 CONT working as an *arbeider*, present at the wedding and consenting to it. He signed with a
2 CONT mark: the act states he could not write.
2 CONT
2 CONT The death entry says only that he was alive on the day of the act. He is nowhere given
2 CONT an age, so this record carries no birth date — his son was 21, which places him loosely
2 CONT in the 1780s or 1790s and no closer than that.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER — his own marriage to [[elisabeth_deyn]], which would name his parents, and
2 CONT which the Sint-Stevens-Woluwe or Zaventem registers should hold for roughly 1815–1824.
2 CONT Neither has been searched for him.
2 CONT
2 CONT ACT READ (2026-07-26): named again seven years later, as father of the bride in his
2 CONT daughter [[anna_maria_bossin]]'s marriage act — Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 9, 1 December 1853
2 CONT (S22). Still at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, present and consenting, still unable to write, and
2 CONT his trade written *daglooner* where the 1846 act had said *arbeider*. The two words say the
2 CONT same thing; the record keeps each act's own.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is therefore alive on 1 December 1853, and the death bound moves from 1846 to that date.
2 CONT His known children go from one to two.
2 CONT
2 CONT DOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`, in the sweep of docs/research-log.md §52.
2 CONT Nothing here was refuted and no fact changed. What changed is the honest name for the
2 CONT evidence: every act behind this record is an AGATHA act analysis — the Rijksarchief's own
2 CONT Demogen transcription — and AGATHA holds no scan for any of them. `doc` means an act or
2 CONT its image was actually read. None was. The register images are the named next step.
1 SOUR @S25@
