1 REFN augusta
2 TYPE project-id
1 NAME Augusta /Vanstechelman/
2 GIVN Augusta
2 SURN Vanstechelman
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 14 MAR 1882
2 PLAC Mariakerke
1 DEAT
2 DATE 4 OCT 1922
2 PLAC Mariakerke
1 FAMS @F20@
1 FAMC @F58@
1 NOTE One of fifteen siblings; her marriage to Petrus Bundervoet is the Vanstechelman–Bundervoet junction.
2 CONT
2 CONT CORROBORATED (July 2026). A Familiekunde Vlaanderen Westkust memorial-card record
2 CONT gives birth 14 March 1882 at Mariakerke, death 4 October 1922 at Mariakerke, and spouse
2 CONT Petrus Bundervoet — every field as held here, where before this rested on the stechec
2 CONT tree alone. Found by harvesting the surname from Open Archives, not by searching for her.
2 CONT
2 CONT Stays `sup`: an index transcription of a card, not an image read.
2 CONT
2 CONT CORROBORATED FROM CIVIL REGISTRATION (July 2026), not only from a memorial card. Her
2 CONT parents [[petrusjacobus_v]] and [[clementia_w]] appear together as the parents on three of
2 CONT her siblings' Oostende acts ([[fs-wvl-bs]]) — a couple attested repeatedly in the registers
2 CONT rather than asserted once by a tree.
2 CONT
2 CONT Three of her siblings surface in West-Flemish civil registration, each in an act naming
2 CONT both parents — which is what corroborates the parentage:
2 CONT
2 CONT - **Henricus Emilius Vanstechelman**, b. 1877, died Oostende 17 January 1941, married
2 CONT   Alicia Mathildis St Martin;
2 CONT - **Leontius Ivo Vanstechelman**, married at Oostende 20 August 1922 to Lucia Amelia Maene;
2 CONT - **Paula Mathilde Vanstechelman**, married at Oostende 11 May 1924 to Alberic Luciaan Delrue.
2 CONT
2 CONT All three now have records — [[henricus_e_v]], [[leontius_v]] and [[paula_v]] — at `sup`,
2 CONT citing the acts that name them. They were briefly left as a frontier on the grounds that no
2 CONT image had been read, which was the wrong test: adding a person a document names as somebody's
2 CONT child is transcription, not identification, and the rule about two independent identifiers
2 CONT guards the second thing. A civil act naming both parents is stronger evidence than the member
2 CONT trees several people here were added from.
2 CONT
2 CONT How they were found is worth recording: searching the mother's surname. Vanstechelman is
2 CONT common at Oostende, Wagebaert is not, so querying the rare maternal name isolates this one
2 CONT household out of the parish.
1 SOUR @S26@
