1 NOTE SPELLING CORRECTED (July 2026): *Antonia*, not "Antoina". the Kraainem marriage act of 3 February 1902 (akte nr. 2, [[S5]]) names her as the
2 CONT bridegroom's mother, which is also what fixes her as the mother of [[jbgeorgius]]. The act
2 CONT gives her no dates and no occupation, so none is recorded — her own birth and marriage
2 CONT acts are the frontier.
2 CONT
2 CONT DOCUMENTED (July 2026) by her own marriage act — Kraainem, 20 June 1872 — which names
2 CONT her as the bride, born at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, and gives **both her parents**:
2 CONT Guilielmus Bossin and Anna Catharina Peremans. The tree already had [[guilielmus_bossin]]
2 CONT and [[peremans]] as her parents on a member tree's word; the act settles it.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her mother is written *Anna* Catharina Peremans here, where this tree calls her Joanna
2 CONT Catharina Jacoba. Both forms are recorded, and neither is preferred without a second act.
2 CONT
2 CONT ACT READ (July 2026). The Kraainem marriage act of 20 June 1872 has now been read on
2 CONT AGATHA rather than through an index, and it sharpens this record twice: her birth is
2 CONT **10 January 1849** where the tree had only the year, at **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe**, and her
2 CONT trade at marriage was *fabriekwerkster*. Her parents are named in the act.
2 CONT
2 CONT CORROBORATED (2026-07-26) — and she turns out to be a middle child. FamilySearch's index of
2 CONT the Sint-Stevens-Woluwe civil registers (S24) carries her birth declaration as **11 January
2 CONT 1849**, one day after the birth of 10 January 1849 that her 1872 marriage act gives — the
2 CONT ordinary gap between a birth and its declaration, and an independent confirmation of a date
2 CONT read at the archive. The register writes her forename in the Latin masculine, *Antonius*,
2 CONT where the act she married under says Antonia.
2 CONT
2 CONT The same series gives her two siblings this tree did not have: [[cornelius_bossin]], declared
2 CONT 13 September 1847, and [[ludovica_bossin]], declared 5 October 1853. Both are recorded at
2 CONT `sup`; her own already-documented entry sitting in the middle of the sequence is what makes
2 CONT them safe to add rather than merely plausible.
2 CONT
2 CONT DEATH DATED (2026-07-26): this record held only the year. **Two of her daughters' marriage
2 CONT acts state it exactly** — Kraainem, **7 November 1894** — [[henrica_thumas]]'s of 15 April 1899
2 CONT (S27) and [[misabella_t]]'s of 10 April 1900 (S28), independently, in the field for a dead
2 CONT parent. She was forty-five.
2 CONT
2 CONT Those same acts, with [[jcseraphina_t]]'s of 1892, give her three daughters this tree did not
2 CONT have. In 1892 she is alive and keeping house; by 1899 she is a date in her daughters' acts.
2 CONT
2 CONT DOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`, in the sweep of docs/research-log.md §52.
2 CONT Nothing here was refuted and no fact changed. What changed is the honest name for the
2 CONT evidence: every act behind this record is an AGATHA act analysis — the Rijksarchief's own
2 CONT Demogen transcription — and AGATHA holds no scan for any of them. `doc` means an act or
2 CONT its image was actually read. None was. The register images are the named next step.
