1 REFN coekelberghs
2 TYPE project-id
1 NAME Maria Theresia /Coekelberghs/
2 GIVN Maria Theresia
2 SURN Coekelberghs
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 22 NOV 1848
2 PLAC Bertem
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1919
1 OCCU herbergierster (innkeeper)
1 FAMS @F1@
1 FAMS @F95@
1 FAMC @F36@
1 NOTE Source detail: Geneanet; the 1902 Kraainem marriage act of her daughter Joanna
2 CONT
2 CONT Joanna Vandenbemden's mother; married Henricus Vandenbemden in 1873.
2 CONT
2 CONT DOCUMENTED (July 2026) as the bride's mother in the Kraainem marriage act of 3 February 1902 (akte nr. 2, [[S5]]): living at Kraainem,
2 CONT *herbergierster*, the occupation already held here. The act makes her the mother of
2 CONT [[vandenbemden]] and the wife of [[hendrik_vdb]].
2 CONT
2 CONT GRAFTED (2026-07-26): her own marriage act — **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 6, 24 April 1873** —
2 CONT names her parents as [[jb_coekelberghs]], *landbouwer* of Bertem, and [[anna_haesaerts]],
2 CONT *landbouwster* of Bertem, both present and both consenting. It also gives her birth to the
2 CONT day, **Bertem, 22 November 1848**, where this record held only the year; her trade at
2 CONT twenty-four, *dienstmeid*; and the commune the marriage was passed in, which neither
2 CONT spouse's record carried.
2 CONT
2 CONT The link does not rest on her name. Two identifiers already in this tree agree with the
2 CONT act exactly: the marriage date 24 April 1873, and her husband's birth — Everberg,
2 CONT 19 August 1849, to the day. A third bridge pins her across thirty years: her **1903
2 CONT Kraainem remarriage act** names the same parents again, and names her late first husband
2 CONT as *Henricus August Vandenbemden, overleden Kraainem 12/08/1889* — the same death date
2 CONT **and** the same commune that the 1902 act established when it corrected this tree's
2 CONT Sint-Stevens-Woluwe to Kraainem. Three acts, thirty years apart, triangulating.
2 CONT
2 CONT That 1903 act also gives her a second marriage this tree did not have, to the widower
2 CONT [[henricus_vanesch]], and her parents' deaths: Bertem, 8 January and 19 November 1880.
2 CONT
2 CONT DOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`. Nothing about her was refuted — the evidence
2 CONT grew. The demotion is about what the evidence *is*: every act behind this record, [[S5]]
2 CONT included, is an AGATHA act analysis, the Rijksarchief's own Demogen transcription, and not
2 CONT one of them has a scan on AGATHA or Open Archives. `doc` means an act or its image was
2 CONT read. None was. See docs/research-log.md §51 — this record is one of about twenty carrying
2 CONT the same overstatement, and the sweep is a pass of its own.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER — the register image for the 1873 act, which would move this whole cluster to
2 CONT `doc`. FamilySearch's microfilm for Sint-Stevens-Woluwe civil registration 1871–1875 is
2 CONT digitised and browsable as DGS **004712751, item 2, images 317–768**; the specific image
2 CONT for act nr. 6 has not been located within it. Her 1919 death is still a Geneanet claim and
2 CONT nothing found in this pass touches it.
1 SOUR @S41@
2 QUAY 2
