1 REFN cornelius_pardon59
2 TYPE project-id
1 NAME Cornelius /Pardon/
2 GIVN Cornelius
2 SURN Pardon
1 SEX U
1 BIRT
2 DATE 5 SEP 1859
2 PLAC Zaventem
1 FAMC @F43@
1 NOTE Named as the child in a civil birth act at **Zaventem, 1859-09-05**, which gives both
2 CONT parents — [[franciscus_pardon]] and [[anna_maria_bossin]] — and so places this person in the tree by the act rather than
2 CONT by a name. The father, present as *aangever*, is a *papiermakerswerkman* living at Zaventem —
2 CONT his trade at his 1853 marriage was *dienstbode*, so it had already changed by this second child.
2 CONT
2 CONT The act is held in the harvested corpus and reached through Open Archives:
2 CONT https://www.openarchieven.nl/abl:17bb266b-3a29-270a-469d-40e86d230954
2 CONT
2 CONT **The family's move from Sint-Stevens-Woluwe to Zaventem, between this birth and the two births
2 CONT before it, is one migrating family and not two couples.** [[henricus_pardon54]] (1854) and
2 CONT [[joanna_pardon56]] (1856) were born at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe; this child (1859) and
2 CONT [[maria_pardon63]] (1863) at Zaventem. Three of the four — Henricus, Joanna Coleta and Maria
2 CONT Thérèsia — are double-attested by their own later Zaventem marriage acts, and each of those three
2 CONT independently names the same father, "Frans/Franciscus/Jan Frans Pardon, deceased Zaventem
2 CONT 18/07/1874," and the same mother, Anna Maria Bossin (`zaventem-pardon-children-marriages-1877-1886`).
2 CONT That carries the identity across the move rather than starting a second family at the new
2 CONT address; this child alone has no later marriage act found in the held corpus, so is
2 CONT single-attested by the birth act, which is already two independent identifiers (both parents'
2 CONT names and birthplaces) beyond the shared surname.
2 CONT
2 CONT `sup`: an indexed act, not the register image. **No `sex` is recorded**, because the harvested
2 CONT mention carries only the relation role and never a sex, and this project does not read a sex
2 CONT off a forename.
