1 REFN cornelius_peremans
2 TYPE project-id
1 NAME Cornelius /Peremans/
2 GIVN Cornelius
2 SURN Peremans
1 SEX M
1 FAMC @F101@
1 NOTE A second sibling for [[peremans]]. His marriage banns were published at **Zaventem on 21 April
2 CONT 1844** (S30), naming his parents as [[egidius_peremans]] and *Theresia Verelst* — the short
2 CONT form of [[joanna_verelst]]'s name, which is how half this family's acts write her.
2 CONT
2 CONT The timing is worth noticing. His father had been dead seven years and his mother **four
2 CONT months** — she died on 19 December 1843. He married in the spring after burying her, and his
2 CONT sister [[peremans]] married in the February after that, at twenty-one and orphaned on both
2 CONT sides.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anchored the same way as [[mjosephina_peremans]]: the record itself gives no place, and the
2 CONT commune comes from the title of the volume the page sits in. Zaventem is where both his parents
2 CONT died and where two of his sisters married.
2 CONT
2 CONT **His wife is not recorded, deliberately.** The index lists three more people in the same
2 CONT document — *Lambertus van der Pelen*, *Maria Catharina van der Vaeren* and *Maria Anna van der
2 CONT Vaeren* — and states the role of none of them. Maria Anna is the likeliest bride and the other
2 CONT two the likeliest parents, but the surnames do not line up in the obvious way, and guessing
2 CONT which of three unlabelled people someone married is exactly the kind of invention this project
2 CONT forbids.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER: the marriage act itself, which would name the bride and both sets of parents; and his
2 CONT own birth act at Zaventem, probably in the 1810s or 1820s.
