1 NAME Henricus Augustinus /Vandenbemden/
2 GIVN Henricus Augustinus
2 SURN Vandenbemden
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 19 AUG 1849
2 PLAC Everberg
1 DEAT
2 DATE 12 AUG 1889
2 PLAC Kraainem
1 OCCU dienstbode (servant)
1 FAMS @F1@
1 FAMC @F120@
1 NOTE Source detail: Geneanet; daughter Joanna's 1902 Kraainem marriage act
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Everberg; married Maria Theresia Coekelberghs in 1873; died young (1889) at Kraainem. Named in daughter Joanna's 1902 marriage act.
2 CONT
2 CONT CORRECTED (July 2026). This record gave his death place as Sint-Stevens-Woluwe.
2 CONT the Kraainem marriage act of 3 February 1902 (akte nr. 2, [[S5]]), which names him as the bride's late father, states **Kraainem** — with the death
2 CONT date, 12 August 1889, agreeing exactly. The same man, the wrong commune; the place is now
2 CONT as the act has it. He had died thirteen years before his daughter married.
2 CONT
2 CONT GRAFTED and CORRECTED (2026-07-26): his own marriage act — **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 6,
2 CONT 24 April 1873** — names his parents. This record carried them as a Geneanet claim flagged
2 CONT *to verify*: "Joannes Baptista Vandenbemden × Agatha Langa". The act gives
2 CONT [[jb_vandenbemden]] and [[elisabeth_langes]] — so the father was roughly right, the mother
2 CONT was **Elisabeth Agatha**, not Agatha, and the surname was **Langes**, not Langa. The
2 CONT Geneanet reading is retired. The act also gives his trade at twenty-three, *dienstbode*,
2 CONT and the commune the marriage was passed in.
2 CONT
2 CONT Two identifiers carry it beyond the surname: his birth, Everberg 19 August 1849, agreeing
2 CONT with this record to the day, and the marriage date 24 April 1873, likewise. His death —
2 CONT Kraainem, 12 August 1889 — is then confirmed a *third* time by his widow's 1903 remarriage
2 CONT act, which names him as her late husband with that date and that commune.
2 CONT
2 CONT Only his mother is recorded as present and consenting. His father is a bare name with no
2 CONT residence, no trade and no consent, which is the register's usual shape for a parent
2 CONT already dead; nothing is recorded from that silence beyond noting it on
2 CONT [[jb_vandenbemden]].
2 CONT
2 CONT DOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`, for the same reason as [[coekelberghs]]:
2 CONT every act behind this record is an AGATHA act analysis and none of them has a scan. See
2 CONT docs/research-log.md §51.
2 CONT
2 CONT RESOLVED (2026-07-26): all seven further Sint-Stevens-Woluwe births the held corpus names for
2 CONT this couple, 1873–1886, are now recorded — [[lodewijk_bemden73]], [[victor_bemden74]],
2 CONT [[felix_bemden76]], [[karel_vandenbemd78]], [[jan_bemden80]], [[adela_bemden84]] and
2 CONT [[julius_vandenbemd86]] — each by an act naming both parents' exact birthplaces (father Everberg,
2 CONT mother Bertem), matching this couple's own recorded birthplaces. Felix and Jan are additionally
2 CONT double-attested by their own Kraainem marriage acts (1897 and 1900), which independently repeat
2 CONT their births and this couple's death and occupation facts twenty years on.
2 CONT
2 CONT An eighth candidate, *Appolonia* (b. Sint-Stevens-Woluwe 1877-01-28), was checked and
2 CONT **REJECTED**: the act names a different couple, Willem Edouard Vandenbemden x Maria Anna
2 CONT Vandenhoven — see the frontier on [[jb_vandenbemden]] for that rival family, a lead for a
2 CONT brother rather than a graft here. The record this tree briefly carried for that child,
2 CONT `data/people/appolonia_vandenbemd77.md`, has been removed.
1 SOUR @S41@
2 QUAY 2
