1 REFN jb_vandenbemden
2 TYPE project-id
1 NAME Jan Baptist /Van den Bemden/
2 GIVN Jan Baptist
2 SURN Van den Bemden
1 SEX M
1 FAMS @F120@
1 NOTE Father of the groom in his son [[hendrik_vdb]]'s marriage act — Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 6,
2 CONT 24 April 1873.
2 CONT
2 CONT **What the act does not say about him is the informative part.** His wife
2 CONT [[elisabeth_langes]] is given a residence, a trade and the words *present and consenting*;
2 CONT he is given a name and nothing else — no commune, no occupation, no consent. That is the
2 CONT register's usual shape for a parent already dead, and it is why this record carries no
2 CONT death entry at all rather than a `raw` note claiming he was alive: a bare name is not a
2 CONT statement either way, and inventing "alive on 24 April 1873" from silence would be exactly
2 CONT the guess the grammar has no syntax for.
2 CONT
2 CONT He confirms — and corrects — an unverified Geneanet claim this tree had been carrying on
2 CONT his son's record, which named him *Joannes Baptista Vandenbemden*. The act's own spelling
2 CONT is *Jan Baptist Van den Bemden*, and it is followed here.
2 CONT
2 CONT `sup`: an AGATHA act analysis, not the register image.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER — his own marriage to Elisabeth Agatha Langes, which the Everberg or Kortenberg
2 CONT registers should hold for roughly 1840–1849 and which would name his parents; and his
2 CONT death, which on the reading above falls before April 1873. Two Van den Bemden witnesses
2 CONT stood at his son's wedding — *Lodewijk*, 40, daglooner of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, and
2 CONT *Willem*, 26, landbouwer of Schaarbeek — and one of them is likely his son or his brother.
2 CONT Neither is grafted: the act states no kinship for either.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER — **Willem Edouard Vandenbemden**, a second Everberg-born Vandenbemden of much the same
2 CONT age, living in the same commune as [[hendrik_vdb]], and a strong lead for a brother — but not
2 CONT grafted. A Sint-Stevens-Woluwe birth act of 28 January 1877 names him as the declaring father: 28
2 CONT years old, born at Everberg, *daglooner*, married to Maria Anna Vandenhoven, born at Kraainem
2 CONT (https://www.openarchieven.nl/abl:2c0d71d9-be5c-fa20-000f-fd03a9ac2403). That act was briefly
2 CONT misread as [[hendrik_vdb]]'s own child, Appolonia — see the correction on his record. The same
2 CONT couple recurs as parents of a further child, Frans Vandenbemden (b. Kraainem 1872-09-28), in
2 CONT Frans's own 1897 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe marriage act, which also gives Willem Edouard's death:
2 CONT Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 20 March 1891
2 CONT (https://www.openarchieven.nl/abl:caefee09-568f-04b7-f115-22d4b7730684). Not grafted: the 1877
2 CONT act states no kinship between Willem Edouard and [[hendrik_vdb]], and a shared birthplace
2 CONT (Everberg) and a shared decade of birth is one identifier, not the two this project requires
2 CONT before a link is made. Neither act names Willem Edouard's own parents, so there is not yet a way
2 CONT to test the "brother" reading directly.
