2 DATE 10 JUN 1857
2 PLAC Grez-Doiceau
1 FAMS @F84@
1 FAMC @F144@
1 NOTE DOCUMENTED (July 2026) by her own death act — Grez-Doiceau, 10 June 1857, the year this
2 CONT record already held — which gives two things the tree did not have at all: her **parents**,
2 CONT Guillaume Joostens and Jeanne Marie Deconninck, and her **birthplace**,
2 CONT Woluwe-Saint-Lambert. Her husband Georges Thumas is named as the survivor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her parents are a documented frontier rather than a graft: they are named here plainly, and
2 CONT adding them is the obvious next step, but neither has a record yet and nothing beyond this
2 CONT act has been read about them.
2 CONT
2 CONT ACT READ (July 2026). Her own death act — Grez-Doiceau, akte nr. 35, registered 11 June
2 CONT 1857 and giving the death as the **10th** — read at the archive and saved
2 CONT ([[joostens-1857-death-grez-doiceau]]). It fixes the day where this record had only the year,
2 CONT confirms her birthplace of Woluwe-Saint-Lambert from the act itself, gives her occupation as
2 CONT *ménagère*, and names her parents [[guillaume_joostens]] and [[jeanne_deconninck]], who until
2 CONT a pass ago were not in this tree at all.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her stated age of 47 puts her birth in 1809–10, which agrees with the 1810 held here.
2 CONT
2 CONT DOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`, in the sweep of docs/research-log.md §52.
2 CONT Nothing here was refuted and no fact changed. What changed is the honest name for the
2 CONT evidence: every act behind this record is an AGATHA act analysis — the Rijksarchief's own
2 CONT Demogen transcription — and AGATHA holds no scan for any of them. `doc` means an act or
2 CONT its image was actually read. None was. The register images are the named next step.
1 SOUR @S72@
