1 NAME Marie-Louise /Van Bergen/
2 GIVN Marie-Louise
2 SURN Van Bergen
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1842
2 PLAC Waasmunster
1 DEAT
2 DATE 22 NOV 1888
2 PLAC Oostende
1 OCCU werkvrouw
1 FAMS @F22@
1 FAMC @F154@
1 NOTE Mother of Louise Marie Bocklandt (1877, Hamme O-Vl). Full name Maria Louisa Van Bergen,
2 CONT 1842-1888. Her parents were Joannes Franciscus Van Bergen (1815-1898) × Ida Vermandel
2 CONT (1825-1865).
2 CONT
2 CONT CITATION REPAIRED (2026-07-26), replacing the §52 downgrade. Her own death act — Oostende
2 CONT nr. 721, 23 November 1888 ([[agatha-oostende-1888-death-maria-louisa-vanbergen]]) — names
2 CONT her father **Joannes Franciscus Vanbergen**, living at Hamme, *metser*, her mother **Ida
2 CONT Vermandel**, "overleden te Hamme", and her partner **Eduardus Bocklandt**. CONFIDENCE STAYS
2 CONT `sup`: AGATHA serves this act only as an "analyse van akte" (index transcription), not the
2 CONT register image.
2 CONT
2 CONT A BIRTHPLACE CORRECTION. The act states her *geboorteplaats* as **Waasmunster**, not Hamme.
2 CONT The family prose elsewhere says Hamme throughout, but that was her father's residence at
2 CONT the time of her death, not her own birth commune. Her own birth act, and her parents' own
2 CONT marriage, therefore belong in the **Waasmunster** registers rather than Hamme's;
2 CONT [[ida_vermandel]]'s record carries the same pointer, and is high on the research queue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death date and act date differ by one day: she died 22 November 1888, the act was drawn up
2 CONT 23 November — ordinary Belgian declare-the-day-after practice, not a conflict.
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation *werkvrouw* is from this 1888 act, at Oostende; the 1880 Hamme death act of her
2 CONT son Ludovicus ([[fs-hamme-1880-death-ludovicus-bocklandt]]) calls her *spinster*, aged 39,
2 CONT eight years earlier — the field keeps the later trade, this note keeps the earlier one.
2 CONT
2 CONT A SISTER (2026-07-26): [[paulina_vdberghe]], born at Hamme about 1849, whose own 1882
2 CONT marriage act names the same parents — and dates their mother's death to the day that
2 CONT [[ida_vermandel]]'s own death act gives independently. Two more probable siblings, Josephus
2 CONT (b. 1852) and Henricus (b. 1861), are named as frontiers on their mother's record and are
2 CONT not grafted: they rest on a name index and their acts have not been read.
1 SOUR @S95@
