1 REFN paulina_vdberghe
2 TYPE project-id
1 NAME Paulina /Van Den Berghe/
2 GIVN Paulina
2 SURN Van Den Berghe
1 SEX U
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1849
2 PLAC Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen)
1 FAMS @F187@
1 FAMC @F154@
1 NOTE An elder sister of [[marie_vanbergen]], and the first of that generation this tree has
2 CONT besides her. Her marriage act — **Hamme, 18 May 1882**, read as the register image — names
2 CONT her as *meerderjarige dochter van* **Joannes Franciscus Van Den Berghe**, *metser*, sixty-five
2 CONT years old, living at Hamme, present at the wedding and consenting, *en van wijlen* **Ida
2 CONT Vermandel, overleden te Hamme den eenen twintigste Juny achttien honderd vyf en zestig**.
2 CONT
2 CONT **What carries the graft is that death date.** Twenty-one June 1865 at Hamme is exactly what
2 CONT [[ida_vermandel]]'s own death act says — a different act, a different clerk, seventeen years
2 CONT apart, and neither knowing about the other. The second identifier is the father's trade,
2 CONT *metser*, which is the same trade [[jan_van_bergen]] is given in [[marie_vanbergen]]'s 1888
2 CONT Oostende death act. Her forename and her mother's surname are not doing the work here.
2 CONT
2 CONT **It also settles a spelling that was blocking three grafts.** The register writes this
2 CONT family **Van Bergen** in 1865 — Ida's death act, and the 1865 alphabetical *tafel*, which
2 CONT files it among Van-acker, Van-Bergen, Van-Bochstael, Van-Bogaert, so it is not a *Van den*
2 CONT name there. The 1882 index writes **Van Den Berghe**. That difference was the reason three
2 CONT possible siblings sat unrecorded, because a clerk's drift and two families sharing an
2 CONT unusually rare wife's surname look identical from an index. Reading the act resolved it as
2 CONT one family. The surname here follows the act that was actually read.
2 CONT
2 CONT The act records her as a widow before this marriage. Her first husband's forename is not
2 CONT confidently legible on the image and no name is recorded from it — a name read at the edge
2 CONT of legibility is a guess, and this project has no field for one.
2 CONT
2 CONT `doc`: the register image was read, by stitching the deep-zoom tiles on the
2 CONT `sg30p0.familysearch.org` origin. Her birth year comes from her stated age and is not itself
2 CONT proved by an act.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER — her own Hamme birth act of about 1849, which would give her birth to the day;
2 CONT and her first marriage, which the Hamme registers should hold before May 1882.
1 SOUR @S101@
2 QUAY 3
