1 FAMS @F14@
1 NOTE FRONTIER above — great-great-grandfather of Elodia Bostyn on the Perquy line. Dates not yet recovered (late-1700s Westkerke area).
2 CONT
2 CONT CITATION REPAIRED (2026-07-26), replacing the §52 downgrade. His daughter
2 CONT [[agatha_stekelorum]]'s death act — Roksem nr. 27, 24 May 1855
2 CONT ([[agatha-roksem-1855-death-agatha-stekelorum]]) — names him as her father, alongside
2 CONT [[helena_denijs]] as her mother and Joannes Perquy as her husband: four of this tree's
2 CONT people in one document, corroborating the tree-stefanieschil claim from a source that does
2 CONT not derive from it. CONFIDENCE STAYS `sup`: AGATHA serves this act only as an "analyse van
2 CONT akte" (index transcription — remark "SCAN 586 GSU", the scan itself not opened).
2 CONT
2 CONT THE ONLY ACT. It is the only act in AGATHA's whole 13.4-million-act index that names a
2 CONT Pieter Stekelorum and a Helena Denijs together, in any spelling — checked against all 37
2 CONT acts naming a "Pieter Stekelorum". Two near-collisions were tested and refuted: act
2 CONT OVWVL_00197046, a Pieter Stekelorum at Jabbeke, is the surviving partner of Joanna
2 CONT Francisca Verplancke — no Denijs anywhere in the act; and act OVWVL_00345955, Varsenare
2 CONT 1797, pairs a Helena **Deschacht**, widow of Stephanus Denys, with a husband named
2 CONT **Joannes** Stekelorum — a different forename, and a former husband's surname rather than
2 CONT her own. Neither touches the Roksem 1855 identification.
