1 FAMS @F158@
1 FAMC @F1@
1 NOTE Source detail: Geneanet (jswaelens); her 1902 Kraainem marriage act
2 CONT
2 CONT A seamstress; married J.B. Georgius Thumas in Kraainem in 1902. Her parents are named in that marriage act. Several of her children died in infancy.
2 CONT
2 CONT DOCUMENTED (July 2026) by the Kraainem marriage act of 3 February 1902 (akte nr. 2, [[S5]]), where she is the bride: born at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe
2 CONT on 15 June 1882, living at Kraainem, *naaister* — the occupation already held here,
2 CONT confirmed word for word — and daughter of Henricus Augustinus Vandenbemden and Maria
2 CONT Theresia Coekelberghs.
2 CONT
2 CONT DOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`, in the sweep of docs/research-log.md §52.
2 CONT Nothing here was refuted and no fact changed. What changed is the honest name for the
2 CONT evidence: every act behind this record is an AGATHA act analysis — the Rijksarchief's own
2 CONT Demogen transcription — and AGATHA holds no scan for any of them. `doc` means an act or
2 CONT its image was actually read. None was. The register images are the named next step.
1 SOUR @S111@
